# Environment Configuration Example

This file shows example configuration values.
Modify `config.sh` in the project root to change settings.

## Application Settings

```bash
# Application name (used for service, user, directories)
APP_NAME="streamlit-starter"

# Application entry point (relative to src/)
APP_ENTRY="app.py"
```

## User & Group (System Installation)

```bash
# Service user and group (for system installation)
# Set to "root" for root execution, or change to any other user for dedicated user isolation
APP_USER="root"
APP_GROUP="root"
```

## Directory Paths

```bash
# System-wide installation directories
APP_DIR="/opt/streamlit-starter"
LOG_DIR="/var/log/streamlit-starter"

# Local development directories
VENV_DIR=".venv"
DEV_LOG_FILE="output.log"
```

## Python Configuration

```bash
# Python executable
PYTHON_CMD="python3"

# Pip executable (with venv)
PIP_CMD=".venv/bin/pip"
```

## Customization Examples

### Change application entry point

If you rename `app.py` to something else:

```bash
APP_ENTRY="app.py"
```

### Change installation directory

For custom installation location:

```bash
APP_DIR="/usr/local/streamlit-starter"
```

## Notes

- `config.sh` is sourced by all scripts automatically
- Changes take effect on next command execution
- Some changes (like APP_DIR) require reinstallation
- Keep `config.sh` in version control to track configuration
